{
  "description": "Answer cache keys and principals (section 7.3). Each case is one read through the cache. Build the client principalKind names from each credential exactly as given, before it is trimmed: the server client from credential for key, the in-app client from the customer token in credential for customer-token, and from key and identityToken for identity. Give it built.baseUrl, asOf (formatted from asOfInput when that is present), visitor for an in-app client, and a custom cache store. Make the read built.route names with built.params: /customers/{id}/entitlements/{feature} is check(feature), /customers/{id}/entitlements is entitlements(), /customers/{id}/plans is plans(), /customers/{id}/pricing is the customer's pricing({ visitor }) and /pricing is the server client's pricing({ visitor }), each passing visitor only when it is not null, and /pricing/features is features(); {id} is the literal me on the in-app client. Compare the key the store is asked for with cacheKey, and the request's Authorization, Entitler-Identity-Token, Entitler-As-Of and Entitler-Visitor headers with requestHeaders, where null means the header is not sent. principal is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of the trimmed credential, or of the trimmed key, a line feed and the trimmed identity token, and serialised is the exact JSON array text whose SHA-256 is cacheKey.",
